      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFlashInfer's CuTe DSL KDA prefill (`recurrent_kda(backend=\"cute-dsl\")`) reads `cu_seqlens` back to the host to plan its routes. It skips that read only when it gets the same int64 tensor object as on the previous call (`kda_chunked_bt16._cu_seqlens_contents`). Our KDA backend passed `query_start_loc` as int32. FlashInfer recasts any int32 `cu_seqlens` to a new int64 tensor on every call (`kda_prefill_cute.py`), so the cached read was never reused and, on routes that read `cu_seqlens`, **every KDA layer did a blocking device-to-host copy**. The host stalled until the GPU stream drained, once per layer.\n\nGLM-5.3-Flash has 34 KDA layers, and FlashInfer prefill is its default KDA prefill backend on SM100/SM103 (the model has a lower-bound gate).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `ForwardMetadata` gains `query_start_loc_int64`. `KDAAttnBackend.init_forward_metadata` builds it once per extend forward, only when the extend kernel sets the new `uses_int64_query_start_loc` class flag. Today only `FlashInferKDAPrefillKernel` sets it.\n- `forward_extend` passes it through, and `FlashInferKDAPrefillKernel` hands it to FlashInfer as `cu_seqlens`. Every KDA layer of a forward therefore gets the same tensor object, so only the first layer reads `cu_seqlens` back to the host.\n- No numerics change: the kernel receives the same offsets, in the same int64 dtype FlashInfer converted them to before.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe kernel inputs are unchanged apart from reusing one int64 tensor, so this change has no accuracy effect. `test/registered/attention/test_kda_prefill_flashinfer.py` passes on GB300 (8 passed).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n**Setup:** GLM-5.3-Flash on 4x GB300, cookbook GB300 High Throughput command.\n\n```\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash --tp-size 4 \\\n  --dsa-prefill-backend trtllm --dsa-decode-backend trtllm --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\\n  --moe-runner-backend flashinfer_trtllm\n```\n\n**Profile: one forward pass, TP0, EXTEND stage**\n\n16-byte `cu_seqlens` device-to-host copies:\n\n| case | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 x 4096 tokens, 34 KDA layers | 34 copies, 20.3 ms host blocked | 1 copy, 0.03 ms |\n| 16 x 1024 tokens | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe 16 x 1024 batch takes a FlashInfer route that does not read `cu_seqlens` on the host, so it is unaffected either way.\n\nBefore, KDA layer 6 of the 1 x 4096 prefill: `recurrent_kda` takes 2.72 ms, 1.96 ms of it blocked in `_cu_seqlens_contents`.\n\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"382\" alt=\"perfetto_before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/790f5d9c-9538-4ac9-a13c-fed384dfb74f\" />\n\nAfter, same layer: 0.71 ms, no host read.\n\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"382\" alt=\"perfetto_after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cc0f3cf-96b2-43be-90b6-935dad1c9318\" />\n\n**End-to-end improvements**\n\n`bench_one_batch_server`, prefill TTFT (median of 3 runs, output length 1, cache flushed per case):\n\n| batch x input | before | after | change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4 x 256 | 64.5 ms | 56.2 ms | -12.9% |\n| 1 x 1024 | 61.3 ms | 55.0 ms | -10.3% |\n| 16 x 4096 | 1198.6 ms | 1134.1 ms | -5.4% |\n\n`bench_serving`, output length 1, `/flush_cache` before every run, same seeds on both sides (mean of 2 runs):\n\n| input, concurrency | before | after | change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2048, 1 | 28.0K tok/s, TTFT 72.0 ms | 32.7K tok/s, TTFT 61.5 ms | +16.9% tok/s |\n| 4096, 4 | 35.6K tok/s, TTFT 459.6 ms | 39.3K tok/s, TTFT 415.3 ms | +10.4% tok/s |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39000180584](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39000180584)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39000180583](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39000180583)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39000180599](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39000180599)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
